  "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
  "label": "User projected onto the textual demand for smiling",
  "description": "The user is projected onto the textual material 'smiiiiiiile' and 'alright girls!', which commands the visual subjects to perform a specific emotional expression. This creates an implicit 'you' projection, where the user is positioned as the one issuing the demand or as the one who is expected to comply with the performative smiling standard. The meme format inherently invites the viewer to imagine themselves as the authority figure or the one being addressed, thus projecting the user's identity onto the text.",
